n/documentation/deployments","created_at":"2017-04-09T17:07:21Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T14:46:35Z","pushed_at":"2025-11-30T16:41:53Z","git_url":"git://github.com/mastodon/documentation.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:mastodon/documentation.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/mastodon/documentation.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/mastodon/documentation","homepage":"https://docs.joinmastodon.org","size":70729,"stargazers_count":1742,"watchers_count":1742,"language":"SCSS","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":984,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":57,"license":{"key":"gfdl-1.3","name":"GNU Free Documentation License v1.3","spdx_id":"GFDL-1.3","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/gfdl-1.3","node_id":"L_kgCoZ2ZkbC0xLjM"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["mastodon"],"visibility":"public","forks":984,"open_issues":57,"watchers":1742,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mastodon/documentation/pulls/1144","html_url":"https://github.com/mastodon/documentation/pull/1144","diff_url":"https://github.com/mastodon/documentation/pull/1144.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mastodon/documentation/pull/1144.patch","merged_at":"2023-01-06T06:54:14Z"},"body":"[The documentation](https://docs.joinmastodon.org/admin/config/#trusted_proxy_ip) previously only indicated that proxies \"on the same machine\" are trusted, but it appears that all private networks are trusted by default. I believe this because:\r\n\r\n- I'm running my web and streaming processes within Docker containers and running Nginx on the Docker host. I believe they communicate over a 172.16.0.0/12 network that Docker creates. I tried looking at logs a bit and it _seems_ like things are working correctly. But if anyone has suggestions on how to verify that my Mastodon processes are recording the correct client IP, please let me know! We could include that advice in this documentation.\r\n- I looked at the source code a bit and it appears that both the streaming and web processes use localhost and the private network ranges. But this is really my first time looking at the Mastodon code and I don't even know Ruby, so please double check me!\r\n  - I believe the streaming processes uses Express JS. I believe it sets the trusted proxy IP [here](https://github.com/mastodon/mastodon/blob/d11d15748cd24342a133221edb3022022b585119/streaming/index.js#L150). Express documents the `loopback` and `uniquelocal` values [here](https://expressjs.com/en/guide/behind-proxies.html).\r\n  - I'm less certain about web. It looks like the env var is parsed [here](https://github.com/mastodon/mastodon/blob/d11d15748cd24342a133221edb3022022b585119/config/environments/production.rb#L44-L45). It looks like `trusted_proxies` will be unset if the env var is unset. And maybe that results in [this check](https://github.com/mastodon/mastodon/blob/main/config/initializers/trusted_proxies.rb) getting bypassed? But it looks like Action Dispatch does it's own check [here](https://api.rubyonrails.org/classes/ActionDispatch/RemoteIp.html)?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mastodon/documentation/issues/1144/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mastodon/documentation/issues/1144/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]